#!args scenario=res://tests/scenarios/Scenario_NoOpeningDiscard.json seed=42
#
# The scenario switch that turns the opening discard off.
#
# With "openingDiscard": true (every shipped scenario, and the default when the key is absent) every
# faction is dealt StaticGameData.OpeningHandSize and must immediately discard OpeningDiscardCount
# before the first turn — see opening_turn.qgc, which pins the other side of this branch.
#
# With it false, GameFlow.StartGame deals straight at HandSize and goes to turn 1. Both halves of the
# rule have to move together: dealing the larger hand without the cut would open every faction over
# the hand cap and dump the surplus at their first DISCARD step.
#
# The absence of the six mandatory prompts is what this test is really about, and it is checked by
# construction rather than by an assertion: there is no `auto` line here, so if the opening discard
# ever fires again, the first `prompt` returns a ForceDiscardHandCards for Germany instead of
# PLAY_CARD and every assertion below it fails.
# Run:  tests/run-cli.sh tests/qgc/opening_discard_disabled.qgc

prompt                      # turn 1, Germany, PLAY_CARD — NOT an opening discard

assert turn == 1
assert faction == GERMANY
assert step == PLAY_CARD

# Seven dealt, none discarded. FAILS (10 / 3) if the flag stopped being read.
assert handsize GERMANY == 7
assert discardsize GERMANY == 0

# Every faction, not just the one whose turn it is.
assert handsize UNITED_STATES == 7
assert discardsize UNITED_STATES == 0

quit
